    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U28-skill-K-HSK3-form-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "HSK 3: form",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "A result compound is a learned word or pattern with a particular result meaning. Shared characters do not prove that a new compound is licensed.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "弄坏",
                "pinyin": "nònghuài",
                "meaning": "damage; break through an action",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "8cf6282f08e55c96b243236930e62f97ddad4d125fff209fdb70c8e7c9cebfd3"
              },
              {
                "text": "修好",
                "pinyin": "xiūhǎo",
                "meaning": "repair successfully",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "eab6c3fd59157f819e6a4e44d04a16479b6bcde7189dc8533d07ff3927bc73b2"
              },
              {
                "text": "找到",
                "pinyin": "zhǎodào",
                "meaning": "to find",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "4cf1501595f0df6d6c92e9f213df020cc4a9a17d1d798e15a13ffbb476c3fe89"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "An object is first damaged through someone’s action. A repair then succeeds. A different missing object is found. Match each introduced result compound to its own event; no new compound is licensed by recombining the visible characters.\nFamiliar meanings available: damage; break through an action; repair successfully; to find."
          }
        ]
      },
